"""
## Purpose and audience
Acceptance oracles for the open remains of
doc/03_plan/compiler/sffi/sffi_universal_admission_next_2026-08-25.md — 51
open `- [ ]` checkboxes across the CPU/HAL/SBI/MMIO/dynload/crypto/async/QUIC/
executable-memory/debug/GPU-owner tranches of the SFFI universal admission
plan. Audience: the SFFI/compiler lane engineers closing this plan.
## Operator workflow
bin/simple test test/03_system/plan_acceptance/sffi_universal_admission_next_spec.spl
## Compatibility and limitations
Tagged in-development: these pin the promised INTERFACE (real functions,
structs, and the canonical `simple.sffi-admission.v1` receipt schema) and
fail until the plan's remaining checkboxes are implemented. Several
checkboxes in the source plan are pure execution/evidence steps gated on
hardware or a toolchain not available on this host (cross-target QEMU/
assembler/sabotage runs, Rust-only unit tests) and have no promised Simple
interface to pin; those are intentionally NOT covered here — see the
skipped list in the delivery report for this file.
## Verification
Every `it` calls a real, grep-verified symbol from `src/` (or reads a real
repo file) and compares its result to a named expected constant computed in
the test itself; none compare a value to itself.
## Troubleshooting
An unresolved `use` import means the promised symbol does not exist yet —
that is itself the finding this in-development spec exists to record.
"""
# @tag:in-development
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/compiler/sffi/sffi_universal_admission_next_2026-08-25.md
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/local/sffi_universal_admission_next_2026-08-25.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/sffi_v2_admission_acceptance.md ;
# doc/05_design/sffi_v2_admission_acceptance.md
# @manual_section: plan-acceptance

# @cover src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/sffi/admission.spl 20%
